WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.888
Severity is useful, but it is not the same as real-world risk.

00:00:05.888 --> 00:00:16.574
Prioritization asks whether the component is affected, whether the condition is reachable or usable in the deployed workload, and what consequence would follow.

00:00:16.574 --> 00:00:24.642
A critical label without deployment context may be less urgent than a lower-scored issue under active exploitation.

00:00:24.642 --> 00:00:34.892
Increase urgency for known exploitation, internet exposure, reachable vulnerable functions, privileged workloads, sensitive data, critical services, weak compensating controls, or broad deployment.

00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:41.216
Consider the image's base ancestry because one fix may address many dependent workloads.

00:00:41.216 --> 00:00:43.179
Affected environment matters.

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:50.811
A production image handling external traffic differs from a private development artifact that is never deployed.

00:00:50.811 --> 00:01:01.497
Development findings still require ownership because old images can be promoted later, copied into another registry, or become part of a future release.

00:01:01.497 --> 00:01:07.821
Validate scanner evidence, distribution backports, package use, and fixed versions before assigning work.

00:01:07.821 --> 00:01:17.198
Document false positives and accepted mitigations so teams do not repeat the same analysis or quietly suppress a valid finding.

00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:25.703
Compensating controls can reduce likelihood or impact through segmentation, disabled features, restricted identity, runtime policy, or service isolation.

00:01:25.703 --> 00:01:34.208
They rarely remove the need to track the underlying vulnerability and should have evidence, ownership, and review dates.

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:40.096
Prioritization should produce an ordered remediation queue, target date, owner, and rationale.

00:01:40.096 --> 00:01:45.112
Reassess when exploitation intelligence, exposure, deployment, or business criticality changes.

00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:54.053
The purpose is to direct limited engineering capacity toward the greatest current risk while keeping every residual item visible.
